{"name": "me-pcr", "id": "65736dcddddec8ded10795bc", "package_types": ["conda"], "summary": "Multithreaded Electronic PCR (in-silico PCR) based on NCBI e-PCR.", "description": "Multithreaded Electronic PCR (me-PCR) was developed by Kevin Murphy at\nChildren's Hospital of Philadelphia. It is described in Murphy et al\n(2004) https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btg466 and was originally\navailable from http://genome.chop.edu/mePCR (defunct). It was based on the\npublic domain NCBI tool e-PCR by Gregory D. Schuler, described in Schuler\n(1997) https://doi.org/10.1101/gr.7.5.541 which was origially availble\nfrom ftp://ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pub/schuler/e-PCR/ (defunct). The final\nrelease of me-PCR was v1.0.6 (2008-02-18), and the author wrote that in\ngeneral NCBI e-PCR should be used instead having been improved greatly\nover the years. The NCBI retired and withdrew the e-PCR webservice and\ncommand line tool on 2017-06-28, suggesting the online-only tool\nPrimer-BLAST instead. However, this is not suitable for offline high\nthroughput usage. See also Jim Kent's isPCR (aslo available in BioConda).\n", "home": "https://web.archive.org/web/20100708193215/http://genome.chop.edu/mePCR/", "public": true, "access": "public", "owner": {"company": "", "location": "", "login": "bioconda", "name": "bioconda", "url": "", "description": "Bioconda is a distribution of bioinformatics software realized as a channel for the versatile Conda package manager.", "created_at": "2015-09-11 22:59:20.880000+00:00", "user_type": "org"}, "full_name": "bioconda/me-pcr", "url": "http://api.anaconda.org/packages/bioconda/me-pcr", "html_url": "http://anaconda.org/bioconda/me-pcr", "versions": ["1.0.6"], "latest_version": "1.0.6", "platforms": {"linux-64": "1.0.6", "osx-64": "1.0.6"}, "conda_platforms": ["linux-64", "osx-64"], "revision": 4, "license": "Public Domain", "license_url": null, "dev_url": null, "doc_url": null, "source_git_url": null, "source_git_tag": null, "app_entry": {}, "app_type": {